          human: 'Aluette (la Vache) is a four-player trick-taking game from VendÃ©e and the coasts of Brittany. Partners sit opposite but do not combine tricks: the team of the individual who wins most tricks (or first to reach that count in a tie) wins the point. Uses a 48-card Spanish-suited pack with a fixed, suit-irrelevant ranking (3s of swords/batons highest down to monsieur/madame lowest). Partners may signal holdings by gestures. Similar to Truc/Put.',
